WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.800
Rey has been using hand-me-downs since the
first moment she touched a lightsaber in The

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.019
Force Awakens, but with the ending of The
Rise of Skywalker, she finally has one of

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:09.520
her own.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.160
Here's what Rey's new lightsaber really means.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.880
In The Force Awakens, Rey first wielded Luke
Skywalker's old lightsaber, which originally

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.280
belonged to Anakin Skywalker.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.940
With Emperor Palpatine finally defeated, Rey
returns to where fans' journey with Star Wars

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:30.500
began 42 years ago: the Lars family moisture
farm on the planet Tattooine, where Luke grew

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.000
up.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.040
Rey buries both Luke's famous lightsaber and
the one Leia used when she was training to

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.710
become a Jedi in the desert near the farm,
before pulling out a new lightsaber she has

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.020
finally forged for herself.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.400
Fortunately for fans, it's not the double-bladed
red lightsaber seen in the trailers for The

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.340
Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.570
The lightsaber that Rey ends up with is a
yellow lightsaber, which is quite rare in

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:54.560
the Star Wars universe.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.160
The yellow lightsaber has most often been
seen in the galaxy far, far away in the hands

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.280
of the Temple Guards on the animated series
Star Wars: The Clone Wars.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.880
Of course, Rey is certainly not joining the
Temple Guard, considering the Jedi temple

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.380
would be fairly empty given the lack of Jedi.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.160
But there's plenty of other symbolism attached
to the yellow lightsaber as well.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.380
Star Wars lore dictates that yellow lightsabers
are carried by the Sentinels, one of the major

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.479
schools of thought within the old Jedi Order
that tries to find balance between the Consulars,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:30.960
which typically bear green blades, and the
Guardians, who normally wield blue lightsabers.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:35.760
With the Sith apparently destroyed by the
end of The Rise of Skywalker, Rey has finally

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.420
brought balance to the Force.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.900
Not only that, but she also appears to be
the only Jedi left, and will have to carry

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.660
the beliefs of them all into the future.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.860
There's also the symbolic decision for Rey
to deviate from what has come before her.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.760
Rey has had quite the journey: she was a poor
scavenger girl abandoned on Jakku by her parents

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.890
who spent most of her life waiting for them
to come back to her, then discovered that

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:04.000
she's Force-sensitive, began training as a
Jedi under Luke Skywalker, joined the Resistance

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.209
and fought against the First Order, found
out she's a Palpatine, and ultimately decided

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:10.200
to take the surname Skywalker as her own.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.700
She had plenty of options from which to choose
in claiming her own lightsaber, she could

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.380
have been blue or green like Luke and Leia,
or red like her cackling electric grandpa.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.470
But in choosing to go a different way with
her lightsaber, Rey chooses her own identity

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.440
separate from her bloodline and her past.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.739
Given the way that Rey grew up, that is, scavenging
as the only way to survive in a desert wasteland,

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.680
she knows firsthand how important knowledge
outside the Force can be to survival.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.620
That's just what the Sentinels believed.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.800
All things considered, it makes perfect sense
that she would choose to follow the school

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.900
of thought embodied by the Sentinels in forging
her own lightsaber.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.690
Additionally, it was important for Rey to
put Luke and Leia's lightsabers to rest and

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.620
forge one of her own.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.320
It's a critical part of the process to becoming
a Jedi Master, and until she did so, would

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.920
have rendered her journey incomplete.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:02.840
Star Wars lore also dictates that the kyber
crystals used to create the light in a lightsaber

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.830
are white, and only take on a color once they
have bonded with a Jedi and their path becomes

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:08.320
clear.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.840
The message here is an obvious one: Rey, the
last of the Jedi Order, will embody all that

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.760
the Jedi are.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.940
From the Consulars to the Guardians to learning
real-life skills, Rey carries the entire future

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.370
of the Jedi Order within her, and she must
balance those teachings.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.440
There's another small detail to Rey's new
lightsaber many may have missed.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:32.600
The handle of her saber is made from the staff
she has been carrying around for years, since

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.800
long before she ever left Jakku in the first
place.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.820
It's yet another piece of symbolism, showing
Rey finally leaving her old life behind her,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.680
this time for good.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:46.460
Even in The Rise of Skywalker, we saw that
Rey's education as a Jedi hadn't given her

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.720
the confidence to rely on her strength in
the Force just yet.

00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:54.420
On the training ground, she was unable to
fight off the combat remote with the lightsaber,

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.000
but she disposed of it quickly using a stick
like her staff.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.980
She has always been comfortable with the weapon
in her hand, so it makes perfect sense for

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:06.030
her to bring that relic forward with her into
her new life, without hanging on to any sentimentality

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:06.600
of her past.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:12.531
It's understood that new Star Wars films won't
be telling the tale of the Skywalkers, of

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.960
which Rey is now one by choice thanks to her
final words in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:21.920
Considering The Rise of Skywalker marked the
end of the Skywalker saga, it's not likely

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.200
Rey will be returning in any more movies.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:28.880
This ties in with one of the reasons the Sentinels
don't appear in the nine films already in

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:34.020
existence: those who practiced the beliefs
of the Sentinels believed in concealing themselves

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:39.050
and being inconspicuous, and avoided pulling
out their lightsabers unless absolutely necessary.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.160
With the galaxy seemingly safe at the end
of The Rise of Skywalker, Rey shouldn't need

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.449
to whip out her new weapon that often, and
may even be able to fade into the background

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:49.460
just like the Sentinels.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.480
But who knows?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.680
Maybe she'll teach a whole new order of Jedi
in the future, and we'll meet her students

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:55.880
in a future Star Wars movie.

